<title>USA: Top exporting gates of flowers to NY area, May.</title>
<headline>Top exporting gates of flowers to NY area, May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands exported 78,843 cartons of flowers into the New York tri-state area by way of John F. Kennedy Airport during May, some 26,047 more than in May '96, the US Department of Agriculture said in its monthly import report.</p>
<p>The other two main sources of imports were Israel and Ecuador, both more than doubling what they exported a year earlier.</p>
<p>The detailed USDA statstics included:</p>
<p> Origin of		    May 1997   May 1996</p>
<p> JFK imports		  cartons    cartons</p>
<p> The Netherlands	    78,843     52,796</p>
<p> Israel			 14,914	7,054</p>
<p> Ecuador			11,950	5,734</p>
<p>The imports from the Netherlands and Israel remained for NY markets, but the report showed all the Ecuadorian shipments were forwarded by air to the Ukraine.</p>
